{"amendments":[{"body":"High: the `ProcessParams` kinetic-field rename is incomplete and currently breaks the build. `ProcessParams` now exposes `decomposer_k_doc_mg_c_per_l`, `decomposer_k_do_mg_per_l`, `aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l`, `aob_k_do_mg_per_l`, `nob_k_nitrite_mg_n_per_l`, `nob_k_do_mg_per_l`, `comammox_k_tan_mg_n_per_l`, and `comammox_k_do_mg_per_l` (`crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:56-64`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:72-112`), but `process_preset_to_params` still initializes the deleted field names in `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:347-386`. `cargo test -p tank_harness --lib` now fails with E0560 here. The same stale field names are also still referenced in `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:455-467`, `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:490-506`, and `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs:637-641`, so the core test suite will remain broken even after the scenario mapper is fixed.","rationale":"This is a blocking regression: the branch does not compile cleanly."},{"body":"High: legacy save/preset compatibility is broken for the renamed decomposer/nitrifier half-saturation fields. The runtime now consumes the new fields directly as concentration values (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:100-101`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:167-172`), and the renamed fields only carry serde aliases for the legacy keys (`crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:59-64`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs:75-112`). But the save migration chain only converts plant/algae half-saturation keys (`crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:81-119`, `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs:678-787`), and the preset normalizer likewise only rewrites plant/algae legacy names (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:1186-1293`). That means an old payload such as `aob_k_tan_mg = 0.5` now loads as `0.5 mg N/L` instead of the old `0.025 mg N/L`, which silently changes nitrification/decomposition kinetics for existing saves and legacy TOML presets.","rationale":"This is a silent correctness regression affecting backward compatibility and simulation behavior, not just tests."},{"body":"Medium: the new `envelope_reports_non_finite_values` unit test is built on an impossible condition and will fail once the compile blockers are fixed. The test sets `state.water.ph = NaN` and expects `Envelope::check` to see a non-finite snapshot pH (`crates/tank_harness/src/lib.rs:821-829`), but `TankSnapshot::from_state` recomputes `ph` from `projected_carbonate_equilibrium` instead of copying `state.water.ph` (`crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:232-248`). In an earlier run of `cargo test -p tank_harness`, this exact assertion already failed because `violations` came back empty. The test needs to exercise a field that actually survives into `TankSnapshot`, or the non-finite validation needs to run on raw state rather than snapshot pH.","rationale":"The added test is currently red and will keep CI failing after the build issues above are repaired."}],"summary":"Reviewed the changed save/process/harness code and found three substantive issues: the `ProcessParams` rename was not propagated everywhere and currently breaks compilation, legacy decomposer/nitrifier Ks are not migrated or normalized and will load with the wrong units, and the new harness non-finite-value test is invalid because snapshot pH is recomputed rather than copied from raw state."}